# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: clautolisp-load-dialog-first-id-is-zero -- (load_dialog f) returns 0 for the first dialog file
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-06

* Symptom

In a fresh clautolisp process the first successful =(load_dialog FILE)=
returns =0=. (A missing or unparsable file correctly returns =-1=.)

The Autodesk reference for =load_dialog= says: "A positive integer value
(dcl_id) if successful, or a negative integer if load_dialog can't open
the file." Code that checks =(> dcl_id 0)= -- or =(<= dcl_id 0)= for
failure -- rejects the first dialog file that did load.

* Repro

#+begin_example
$ printf 'p : dialog { label = "P"; ok_only; }\n' > /tmp/p.dcl
$ clautolisp-sbcl --quiet --no-init -x '(princ (load_dialog "/tmp/p.dcl"))'
0
$ clautolisp-sbcl --quiet --no-init -x '(princ (load_dialog "/nonexistent.dcl"))'
-1
#+end_example

* Cause

=clautolisp/autolisp-dcl/source/runtime.lisp=: =*next-dcl-id*= starts at 0
(=fresh-dcl-id= returns the counter before incrementing it).

* Fix

Start the handle counter at 1 (and check that the cadtui DCL bridge and the
subprocess renderer do not assume handle 0). Record the positive-handle
rule in the spec's LOAD_DIALOG entry, whose return value is only "under
host semantics" today.

Found while writing the DCL rows of the alfe parity table
(alfe-clautolisp-backend-semantic-parity.issue): the rows test
=(numberp id)= instead of =(> id 0)= because of this.
